mkchromecast (0.4.4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Build with debhelper.  There is now a debian/ directory, so the package
    can be built with dpkg-buildpackage and rebuilt by anyone who receives
    the source, rather than only by packaging/build-deb.sh.
  * Declare a maintainer who can be reached.  The field held an upstream
    name with a URL where the address belongs, which is not a valid
    Maintainer and is not who builds these packages.
  * Leave the macOS-only trees out of the source package.  archive/ carries
    audiodevice, whose sources say "Copyright 2006 Rogue Amoeba Software,
    LLC. All rights reserved." with no licence grant, and notifier/ states
    its licence only by pointing at a URL.  Neither is used on Linux.
  * Record third-party copyright properly: py-getch under mkchromecast/getch
    and the nodejs streamer each get their own paragraph.

 -- saulusprime <pierno.paolo@gmail.com>  Sat, 22 Aug 2026 09:48:27 +0200
